/*****************************************************************************
    jitSlotT -- THE STEP-2 PATHFINDER RUNG. 2026-08-17.

    Certifies that `*` emits through its gJitEmitter SLOT rather than through
    the `if jitting` gate inside opMultiply.

    ⚠⚠ READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A VALUE ASSERTION AND THINKING IT COVERS THE
    MECHANISM. IT CANNOT. The migration is value-transparent BY DESIGN: a
    migrated multiply and an unmigrated multiply emit the same IR and return
    the same number, because a presence-gated fork is supposed to be invisible
    to everything except the fork. So the products below are necessary and are
    NOT sufficient, and the load-bearing row is the slot COUNT.

    THE NEGATIVE CONTROL, MEASURED 2026-08-17 rather than asserted. The
    jitEmitter registration was removed from the Operators entry for the star
    operator in incant setup, which is read at run time so no rebuild is
    involved, and incant jitJR was run both ways.

        registered      slot count 1    results 6 and 24    degrade 0
        NOT registered  slot count 0    results 6 and 24    degrade 0

    The products are IDENTICAL down the column. Only the count moves. That is
    the H7 bar met and it is also the reason this rung exists in the shape it
    does -- a rung asserting only the product would have stayed green with the
    mechanism removed, which is a green that means nothing.

    WHY A COUNT AND NOT A TRACE LINE. H4. An absence check on a printed marker
    passes on the day somebody deletes the marker. The count is printed
    unconditionally by jitRunAction beside the degrade and compile counts, and
    is compared against a value.

    ⚠ FIRE 2 USES DIFFERENT OPERANDS ON PURPOSE. 42 and 45 differ, so a folded
    constant or a stale result cannot satisfy both. A pair that happened to
    agree would prove nothing -- the injectivity rule, copied from jitJR.

    ⚠ THE JITTED HALF IS FIRST AND THAT ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING, bear-trap 25:
    testing routes by isCoded and an interpreted run consumes it, so an oracle
    placed above the jitted half silently measures the interpreter at exit 0.
*****************************************************************************/

register(JitLadder);
define
    jsA;
    jsB;
    jsOut;
    jsMul code={
        jsOut = jsA * jsB;
        };
    ;

/*  ⚠ THE ASSERTED QUANTITIES ARE THE PRINTED result AND count LINES, NOT A
    FIELD READ. A first draft of this rung printed jsOut after each fire and got
    the string jsOut back both times -- bear-trap 26, a field with no data
    returns its own tag, so the row rendered a plausible name and discriminated
    nothing. The jitted value lives in the RETURN, which jitRunAction and
    jitRefire already print with their values. Assert those three lines:
        jitRunAction result = 42
        jitSlot count = 1
        jitRefire result = 45  */

jsA = 6; jsB = 7;
print "SLOT fire 1 setup : jsA =" jsA " jsB =" jsB " -- want result 42, slot count 1":;
testing(jsMul);

jsA = 5; jsB = 9;
print "SLOT fire 2 setup : jsA =" jsA " jsB =" jsB " -- want result 45, recompile NONE":;
jitRefire();

print "JITSLOT SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
